Meanwhile margin went 24% to 6%. On a revenue base indexed to 100 growing to 115: profit was 24, now it's 6.9. So absolute profit fell roughly 70% while revenue rose. That means total cost went from 76 to 108 — up about 42% against 15% revenue growth. Cost per unit of output has clearly risen, and that's either cost per cup rising or fixed cost being spread over fewer cups per store.

